                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "exemptions": "Subdivision (d) exempts: deed-restricted or subsidized affordable housing; dormitories owned and operated by a higher-education institution or a K-12 school; housing under local rent or price control that limits annual increases to less than the state cap; housing with a certificate of occupancy issued within the previous 15 years (unless a mobilehome); separately alienable property whose owner is not a REIT, corporation, LLC with a corporate member, or mobilehome park management and where the tenants were given the statutory written notice; and a two-unit structure in which the owner occupies one unit as a principal residence (neither unit an ADU or JADU). Subdivision (j) excludes a homeowner of a mobilehome. Dormitory, mobilehome, ADU and new-tenancy-initial-rate conditions are not encoded in coverage_json.",
          "overrides": [],
          "interaction": "Subdivision (m) states that the section does not expand or limit local authority to regulate rents consistent with Civ. Code ch. 2.7 (§ 1954.50 et seq.) and does not authorize local limits not otherwise permissible under that chapter. Local rent-control ordinances with lower caps are exempt under (d)(3). The section is scheduled to be repealed as of January 1, 2030.",
          "effective_date": "2024-04-01",
          "source_doc_id": "D024",
          "conflict_flag": false,
          "conflict_note": null
        },
        {
          "team_rule_id": "r-ffc4cae69322d3f0",
